This package uses the distribution Python, PySide6, pyqtgraph, pyroute2, and
NumPy packages. It does not use the bundled runtime from the GitHub release
archives.

Build a binary package with:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -uc -us

The package installs /usr/share/network-monitor/distro-managed so the in-app
updater does not replace a distribution-managed installation with a GitHub
package. Users should update through apt.

For an official Debian upload, build a signed source package and publish it
through Debian Mentors or ask a Debian Developer to sponsor it. The source
package name is `network-monitor`.
